impl:WI-CACHE.notes:
No files of this work item existed after the crash, so everything was written new. All four modules match their SOC 3.8 port lists exactly.

The random test found four design points, all fixed and each now pinned by a directed test and a planted bug:
- the claim-cycle request for C3;
- the TAS.B deadlock with the ordering gate;
- program order behind queued fills (WTB, WBB, uncached reads);
- fq claimed only after f's accept.

The unit tb has a --watch <PA> trace option for debugging divergences. Scratch files (traces, seed logs, mutant logs) are in agents/scratch/WI-CACHE/. No hardware was used and no git commits were made.

findings.problem:
The unit tb missed the findings above:
- lanes never runs a basic access longer than 63 Bcyc alongside SDRAM or refresh traffic;
- idle checks only gap >= idle, so over-insertion passes;
- BREQ covers only a clean release and return;
- there is no manual reset inside a lock;
- no MPX RDY hold with AnIW = 0;
- the model is never ticked the way Sh4Sys ticks it.

